## Command
job-description-guildleader = Provide guidance or direction to mercenaries and aim to connect solo mercenaries into teams.

## Freelancers
job-description-ls-master-at-arms = Lead the freelancers alone or with other masters at arms, ensure your fellow faction members are obeying engagement rules and coordinate with the other faction's leaders to keep the playing-field interesting.
job-description-ls-freelancer-pirate = Get up close and personal in conflict with the LSRD's enforcers and fight for what is yours, but remember to obey factional escalation laws.
job-description-ls-smuggler = Source anything you can pawn off to other people or your faction's extraction pallet, be it smuggling trading or pilfering from expeditions and combat sites, remember to share with fellow freelancers and help them stay supplied.
job-description-ls-spy = Be the rogue and blend in, complete secret missions delivered to you from the higher ups, try not to get caught, and dont go looking for fights!
job-description-ls-ripper-doc = The backbone of every conflict, treat your fellow freelancers as a priority, then the rest of the sector, ensure both sides of a fight are seen to after a conflict, be them friend or foe.
job-description-ls-escort = Help the faction with sourcing funds, run a resturant, its all up to you, just keep your nose out of the rest of the factions fighting, unless they hire you directly.

## LSRD
job-description-ls-chief-ranger = Lead the LSRD alone or with other chief rangers, ensure your fellow faction members are obeying engagement rules and coordinate with the other faction's leaders to keep the playing-field interesting.
job-description-ls-enforcer = Get up close and personal in conflict with the Freelancer's pirates and fight for what is yours, but remember to obey factional escalation laws.
job-description-ls-retrieval-officer = Source anything you can pawn off to other people or your faction's extraction pallet, be it smuggling trading or pilfering from expeditions and combat sites, remember to share with fellow LSRD members and help them stay supplied.
job-description-ls-detective = Be it through bravado or charm, complete secret missions delivered to you from the higher ups, try not to get caught, and dont go looking for fights!
job-description-ls-corpsman = The backbone of every conflict, treat your fellow LSRD members as a priority, then the rest of the sector, ensure both sides of a fight are seen to after a conflict, be them friend or foe.
job-description-ls-clerk = Help the faction with sourcing funds, run a resturant, its all up to you, just keep your nose out of the rest of the factions fighting, unless they hire you directly.
